<title>POLAND: Polish jeans maker Elpo starts trade up 36.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Polish jeans maker Elpo starts trade up 36.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish jeans garment maker Elpo SA started trading as the first firm on the Warsaw Stock Exchange's free market at 30 zlotys, 36.4 percent higher than its public offering price of 22 zlotys.</p>
<p>The free market was set up for especially small companies with a short audited results history and which do not meet the listing requirements of the main and parallel markets.</p>
<p>Elpo's December initial public was undersubcsribed with underwriters taking 459,680 shares of the 600,000 on offer.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
